<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wang Xianzhi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/878">878</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wang Xianzhi was a salt smuggler who led one of the great rebellions against the late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tang-dynasty">Tang dynasty</a>. Rising in 874 or 875 amid famine and heavy taxes, he was joined by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huang-chao">Huang Chao</a> and raided widely between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-river">Yellow River</a> and the Huai. Offers of office from the court divided him from Huang, and he was defeated and killed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hubei">Hubei</a> in 878, after which Huang Chao led the rebellion.</p></div>
